WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.933
The old way always sounds the same: tabs open, notes scattered, a runner sheet half remembered, and a GM buying time while the table waits for the moment to come back alive.

2
00:00:06.933 --> 00:00:13.865
Chummer6 is built for the instant when preparation has to become play.

3
00:00:13.865 --> 00:00:20.798
It gathers the runner, the crew, the scene, the consequence, and the next decision into one surface that can survive pressure.

4
00:00:20.798 --> 00:00:27.731
You build with the important details in view: gear, chrome, magic, tradeoffs, and every number explained clearly enough that the table can trust it.

5
00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:34.663
You run with momentum: scenes, handouts, opposition, downtime, hooks, fallout, and the next hard choice ready when the room needs them.

6
00:00:34.663 --> 00:00:41.596
When the city answers, it does not answer as decoration.

7
00:00:41.596 --> 00:00:48.529
It answers with heat, factions, jobs, rumors, and consequences the GM can turn into tomorrow night's trouble.

8
00:00:48.529 --> 00:00:55.462
House rules stop living as arguments in old chat logs. Recaps stop dissolving into rumor.

9
00:00:55.462 --> 00:01:02.394
The aftermath becomes signal, and that signal becomes the next run.

10
00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:09.327
From desktop to tablet to phone, from home table to remote night, Chummer6 is for crews who want the world to remember what they did and still be ready when the next door opens.

11
00:01:09.327 --> 00:01:16.260
The product is not trying to replace the table.

12
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:23.192
It is trying to hold the boring parts steady so the dramatic parts can move faster.

13
00:01:23.192 --> 00:01:30.125
The promise is practical: less ceremony, fewer missing details, more time spent in the scene, and a campaign that can keep moving after the dice stop.
